IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `imm-types`
IMPORT `imm-status`
IMPORT `imm-deportation`

-- Immigration Act 2009 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For a person who is not a New Zealand citizen, on a day: are they barred
--    from a visa, unlawfully in New Zealand (and so barred from working),
--    since when, and by when may they appeal; and, if a resident, are they
--    liable for deportation under s 161?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Immigration position` HAS
    `barred from a visa`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `unlawfully in New Zealand`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `barred from working`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `unlawful since`                                    IS A MAYBE DATE
    `last day for a humanitarian appeal`                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `liable for deportation under s 161`                IS A BOOLEAN

@ref ss 9, 15-17, 21, 154, 161
@export default A non-citizen's position under the Immigration Act 2009 (NZ) on a day: whether they are barred from a visa or entry permission (ss 15-17); whether they are unlawfully in New Zealand (s 9) and so may not work (s 21), since when, and the last day for a humanitarian appeal against deportation (s 154); and, for a residence class visa holder, whether they are liable for deportation for offending (s 161). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A Person  @desc Citizenship, visa and entry permission, arrival, visa expiry, convictions, prohibition, deportation, exclusion and special directions
      r IS A MAYBE `Resident facts`  @desc For a residence class visa holder: when they first held it, days imprisoned since, and convictions
      d IS A DATE  @desc The day in question
GIVETH AN `Immigration position`
`the immigration position for` p `, as a resident` r `, on` d MEANS
    `Immigration position` WITH
        `barred from a visa`                    IS `is barred from a visa` p `on` d
        `unlawfully in New Zealand`             IS unlawful
        `barred from working`                   IS `is barred from working by s 21` p
        `unlawful since`                        IS since
        `last day for a humanitarian appeal`    IS
            CONSIDER since
            WHEN JUST s THEN JUST (`the last day for a humanitarian appeal by a person unlawful from` s `, reconsideration confirmed` NOTHING)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        `liable for deportation under s 161`    IS
            CONSIDER r
            WHEN JUST facts THEN `the resident is liable for deportation under s 161` facts
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHERE
        unlawful MEANS `is unlawfully in New Zealand` p
        since MEANS `the day unlawful status starts for` p
